            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0550" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14377: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-26T16:00:00-05:00">November 26, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>307. Tientsin’s 217, November 21, 6 p.m., disorder in area outside the
                    Concessions and adjacent to the Race Club. The Department approves an approach
                    to the Japanese Consul General in the sense indicated in the second substantive
                    paragraph of the telegram under reference but believes that in such approach it
                    would be preferable to stress the matter of protest and to avoid argumentation
                    as to why an approach is being made to the Japanese and also to avoid any
                    statement <pb facs="0551" n="547" xml:id="pg547"/> which might imply assent on
                    our part to assumption by the Japanese of authority at Tientsin.</p>
                <p>Please instruct Tientsin accordingly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
